1
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:05,260
Ever since last night,

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:09,377
I've had this weird feeling that there's
something important I have to do.

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:11,077
But I can't remember what.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,060
Oh, man.

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:15,716
Why do my shoes and bag feel
heavier than usual today?

6
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:20,550
Hold on.

7
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:21,697
This house!

8
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:22,737
How strange.

9
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:26,408
Somehow I ended up walking all
the way back to Rohan's house.

10
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,100
The door's open.

11
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:33,537
I'd like to drop in and thank him for
being such a great host yesterday.

12
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,267
But I'll be late for school.

13
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:37,080
I probably shouldn't.

14
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:40,568
Being an artist, he's
probably still asleep.

15
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,900
He'd be rude to just barge in.

16
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,300
I really shouldn't.

17
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:55,770
Rohan.

18
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,747
He's working with such
a chilling expression.

19
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,157
And for some reason,

20
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:05,097
I can't shake the feeling that being
in this house is actually terrifying.

21
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:06,100
But why?

22
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,397
You finally made it.

23
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,715
It's good to see you.

24
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,120
You're right on time. Huh?

25
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:16,317
Sorry, but could I ask you to
wait there for just a moment?

26
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,960
Two more pages and next week's
manuscript will be complete.

27
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:22,680
It'll only take about 20 minutes or so.

28
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:25,897
Did he say he could finish
two pages in 20 minutes?

29
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,057
That can't be right.

30
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:28,517
I must have misheard him.

31
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:32,257
He couldn't possibly draw two pages from
scratch in such a short amount of time.

32
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,869
And they're for next week?

33
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:39,182
When we were here yesterday, he just finished
drawing the manuscript for this week.

34
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,390
Whoa!

35
00:01:50,473 --> 00:01:52,400
He used the pen right off the bat!

36
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,537
I can't believe what I'm seeing!

37
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:00,837
How can he ink such complex
drawings without sketching first?

38
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:01,750
Whoa,

39
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:03,237
he's not hesitating at all and is even

40
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:06,085
hammering out the
backgrounds at the same time!

41
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,184
His hand movement was so quick!

42
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:22,439
I didn't even have a chance
to make out what he did!

43
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:25,640
No way!

44
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,577
He's beta-coloring by flicking the ink
around like perfectly aimed shuriken,

45
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,257
and somehow he's not leaving
a single stray mark behind!

46
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:33,937
His technique is incredible!

47
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:38,608
To beta-color without a brush takes an
amount of skill I've never seen before!

48
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,357
You've gotta be kidding!

49
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,499
He's already done?

50
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:47,541
It only took him about two minutes
to finish all the beta-coloring.

51
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,857
And it's all thanks to you, Koichi.

52
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:52,580
I am overflowing with creative energy.

53
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,511
My body hungers for more.

54
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,157
I have to keep drawing.

55
00:02:56,240 --> 00:03:00,520
Finishing 19 pages in one night has
been an experience like no other.

56
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:03,920
At this very moment, a
masterpiece is forming.

57
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,691
Your life is astonishing.

58
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:07,300
I don't get it.

59
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:10,320
What is this?

60
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:15,560
Get cracking!

61
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,857
I want the next reality from your past.

62
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,881
Hurry and show me your next page!

63
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,377
I'm aware that your weight decreases
with every page I liberate,

64
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:24,857
but you don't mind, do you?

65
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:28,058
It's a small price to pay
for becoming a masterpiece!

66
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,145
Immortalized for all eternity!

67
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,560
I remember!

68
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
His power is heaven's door!

69
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:39,227
Rohan, you're one of
the enemy's stand-users!

70
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:03,380
Thank you.

71
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:24,260
Thank you.

72
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,340
I'll change you!

73
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:56,700
Well now!

74
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,657
I know it's not done just yet,

75
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:01,537
but this single panel could
be a book hauled by itself!

76
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,450
Fantastic!

77
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:06,522
I feel like I'm maturing, both as
a manga artist and a stand user!

78
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,840
And now to read this page.

79
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:18,570
Interesting.

80
00:05:18,653 --> 00:05:19,483
Unless I'm mistaken.

81
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:25,080
That's Shining Diamond's Josuke
Higashikata, and the Han's Okuyasu Nijimura.

82
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,660
But this doesn't make any sense.

83
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,957
Why would they show up on
my doorstep out of the blue?

84
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:35,097
There's just no way Koichi would
have mentioned me to the two of them.

85
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:36,580
What's going on here?

86
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:38,990
Huh?

87
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:42,926
I don't know how, but
it's Josuke and Okuyasu!

88
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,317
When I didn't show up for school,

89
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,753
they must have noticed I was
missing and tracked me down!

90
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,960
I have to get them to save me!

91
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:52,560
I'm almost there!

92
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:58,420
If I can just open the door, they can
rush in and get me out of this place!

93
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:01,170
Huh?

94
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,530
Oh, hey!

95
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:03,957
This is such a surprise!

96
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,117
What are you two doing here?

97
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:07,847
And for that matter,
how do you even find me?

98
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,700
I'll let it be.

99
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:16,717
Josuke and Okuyasu don't really
interest me at the moment.

100
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,937
For now, I'll finish up the
last two pages for next week,

101
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:23,180
and then I'll procure even
more material from Koichi.

102
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,220
I can hardly contain myself.

103
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:29,637
You came here to watch a
manga artist do his work?

104
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,838
How can this guy afford to
work in such a nice place?

105
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,160
Rohan Kishibe.

106
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,949
Is he famous or something?

107
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,769
Ever heard of him, Josuke?

108
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
I'm not that well-versed in manga.

109
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:43,857
In fact, Hazamada bitched at me for
not knowing anything about Perman.

110
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:44,770
Wait, what?

111
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:48,337
That wasn't even remotely close
to what I wanted to say to them.

112
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:50,420
Why am I blanking all of a sudden?

113
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:51,890
Well,

114
00:06:51,973 --> 00:06:55,557
we saw you staggering around, so we thought
it would be a good idea to tell you.

115
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,934
But it seems like everything is Aqua.

116
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:59,657
I guess we'll leave you to it.

117
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:00,570
Thanks a lot!

118
00:07:00,653 --> 00:07:01,483
What?

119
00:07:01,566 --> 00:07:03,137
Do you want to come inside
and observe with me?

120
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:05,220
Nah, thanks for the offer, though.

121
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:08,088
Being around famous
people makes me nervous.

122
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:10,317
Same, just knowing that
you weren't in there?

123
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,057
fooling around with
some smoking hot chick!

124
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,846
is enough for me, so I'm out.

125
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,800
See you later, Koichi. Bye.

126
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:22,311
Why can't I remember what I wanted to say?

127
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:27,287
I'm sure I was trying to tell them
something really important, but what was it?

128
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:29,880
Now I remember what I wanted to say!

129
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:32,600
I needed them to rescue me!

130
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,540
Yusuke, okuyasu, wait!

131
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:38,000
See you guys at school in a bit. Kay.

132
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,837
Make sure you're not late.

133
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,900
I won't be.

134
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,120
What was that?

135
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,794
That's not what I wanted to say at all!

136
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:53,730
Dammit!

137
00:07:53,813 --> 00:07:55,973
I'm not able to ask my friends for help!

138
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:01,717
We've never gone up against
a stand this terrifying.

139
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,741
It's invincible.

140
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:06,825
I don't think we have nearly
enough power to beat Heaven's door.

141
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:10,480
Ah, I see now.

142
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,460
At the rate he's going,

143
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:17,798
he's going to rip out all my experiences
and leave me a lifeless husk.

144
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:22,225
I sense an infiltrator
has entered the mansion.

145
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:24,397
What did you do while you were downstairs?

146
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,310
Answer me.

147
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:27,960
Ah! Ah!

148
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:33,550
Okuyasu!

149
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,576
Hold it right there!

150
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:37,817
Just keep looking straight ahead, buddy!

151
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,717
You'd better not try anything funny,

152
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,777
or I'll crush you with my
stand, you doodling dipshit!

153
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:44,797
I don't know how you
figured out I was in danger,

154
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,977
Okuyasu, but thank goodness you're here!

155
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,300
You're the best!

156
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:52,157
It appears as though your friend
had a sudden epiphany, Koichi.

157
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,240
I didn't notice it before,

158
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:56,677
but that small cut on your hand must have

159
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:59,417
given away the predicament
you're currently in.

160
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:03,357
You probably scratched yourself on
something while you were crawling.

161
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:06,057
I was so focused on
escaping, I didn't notice!

162
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:09,080
That is what gave it away, right, Okuyasu?

163
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,320
And your stand is the hand.

164
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:15,897
Also, you have a bit of a complex
regarding your dead brother, Keicho.

165
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:18,457
And whenever you try to
make a difficult decision,

166
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:20,857
you wish your brother was
there to do it for you.

167
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:22,120
Isn't that right?

168
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:26,024
Who the hell told you all that?

169
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,160
Speak up, punk!

170
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:30,955
Hey, Koichi, tell me everything
about this guy's stand.

171
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,700
Yeah, he's able to!

172
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,200
I can't do it!

173
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,616
I can't say anything that
put Rohan at a disadvantage!

174
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:41,157
If you catch a glimpse of
even one panel, it's all over!

175
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:43,497
I desperately want to
tell you not to look!

176
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,720
Please, don't look at that manga!

177
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:47,370
Hold it!

178
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,874
Didn't I tell you not to move a muscle?

179
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:51,470
Okuyasu,

180
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,837
you were of no concern to me at first,

181
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:56,317
but that changed the moment
you entered this house.

182
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,960
Now you'll serve as another of my muses.

183
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:02,210
Bastard!

184
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:06,840
What the hell?

185
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:07,980
He's really fast!

186
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:13,870
Okuyasu!

187
00:10:15,660 --> 00:10:17,220
What's going on?

188
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:22,600
Josuke Higashikata, I know
you're hiding over there.

189
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,590
Okuyasu!

190
00:10:35,673 --> 00:10:38,717
What the hell is up with
this freaky-ass manga artist?

191
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:39,630
Silence.

192
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:45,037
Now then, Koichi, if you
don't mind, I have a question.

193
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:50,360
Why do you think Josuke Higashikata is
choosing to remain hidden behind that door?

194
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:52,870
Hmm?

195
00:10:52,953 --> 00:10:54,095
So what do you think?

196
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,520
Why won't he show himself, Koichi?

197
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,100
Well, if I had to guess,

198
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:02,937
I'd say he's laying low so he won't
accidentally catch a sight of your manga!

199
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:06,380
My thought's exactly
how very astute of you.

200
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:10,257
Okuyasu knew nothing about
the power of my Heaven's Door,

201
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:13,105
so he fell from my trap
hook, line, and sinker.

202
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:17,622
But in doing so, he exposed the
true nature of my stand to Josuke,

203
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,369
causing him to take cover.

204
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:21,177
I feel that I am somewhat...

205
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:25,260
No, at this point it would appear
I'm at a significant disadvantage.

206
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:30,680
However, I believe that Josuke has an
ulterior motive for choosing to remain hidden.

207
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:32,840
What do you think that is?

208
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:37,577
At any rate, this game of cat and
mouse has gone on long enough.

209
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:41,457
I suppose I'll have to resort to other
means to smoke him out of his hiding place.

210
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:45,897
He's only hiding because he wants to
figure out the best way to kick your ass!

211
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,921
You're probably right about that.

212
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:50,667
But that wasn't the
answer I was looking for.

213
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,597
No matter, though, I think I've got it.

214
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:56,857
Our dear hero Josuke is
contemplating whether

215
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:59,537
he should flee the mansion
all by his lonesome...

216
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:00,777
some friend he is.

217
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:01,690
You're wrong!

218
00:12:01,773 --> 00:12:03,077
Josuke would never leave us behind!

219
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,780
Right you are, Koichi. Huh?

220
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:06,932
According to your files,

221
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,417
Josuke Higashikata has
far too much character

222
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,794
to even think about abandoning you two.

223
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:15,317
But due to the dynamic nature
of a manga artist's work,

224
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,997
they tend to consider every
conceivable possibility?

225
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,880
at every conceivable moment.

226
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:23,280
So in the situation we
now find ourselves in,

227
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:26,157
what course of action will
our protagonist employ?

228
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,070
Let's see.

229
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:30,897
Perhaps Josuke could flee with
knowledge of my stand's power,

230
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:33,177
which would be quite the dilemma for me.

231
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:36,637
You know, running away might
be the best thing he could do!

232
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:37,877
He could go and get Jotaro!

233
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,277
And if he told Yukako
what happened to you,

234
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,897
I'm sure she'd be angry
enough to help us out.

235
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:44,357
I'd rather not see her again.

236
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,969
But we could use her hair.

237
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:48,897
Josuke, get out of here and
tell them what's going on!

238
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:50,000
You imbeciles!

239
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:53,237
I explained all of that to you
exactly so it wouldn't happen.

240
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:57,717
And I doubt you'd be so quick to prompt
Josuke if you knew what was written in you.

241
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:02,217
Koichi, I'm giving you my express permission
to explain the content of my missive.

242
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,130
Let's hear it.

243
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:06,517
There's no way!

244
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,437
You can't be serious!

245
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:08,920
Hey, out with it.

246
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:10,217
What did he write, Koichi?

247
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:12,620
How can he do that? It's sick.

248
00:13:13,220 --> 00:13:15,749
He's completely trapped
us in this mansion.

249
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:18,837
It doesn't matter what we do,
we're never getting out of here.

250
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:23,332
Man, that's why I'm asking what the
hell this sickle run on my arm, Koichi.

251
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:30,080
Burn myself to death?

252
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:32,617
That's why I said we're
never getting out of here.

253
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:36,700
You'll kill yourself if Josuke so
much as lifts a finger to help us.

254
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:39,000
Hey, wait a second.

255
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:41,398
He thinks I'll burn myself to death?

256
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:43,700
That's total crazy talk!

257
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:47,507
As if I'd ever do something as
messed up as setting myself on!

258
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:49,731
That's just it, you will!

259
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:52,331
We're completely incapable of defying him!

260
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:54,457
Come on, right hand, knock it off!

261
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,600
This is so wrong!

262
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,540
So you've come out.

263
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,137
Like he really had a choice!

264
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:08,677
He was basically dragged out of here
because he couldn't bear to hear us suffer.

265
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:11,260
Oh, that's a rather childish move.

266
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:13,557
But closing your eyes could be effective.

267
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:15,597
There's nowhere to run
in this cramped room.

268
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:17,157
If he managed to knock me out?

269
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,537
Heaven's Door would release its grip.

270
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:20,738
and Okuyasu wouldn't commit suicide.

271
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:23,010
Josuke, help!

272
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:28,937
Closing his eyes is simple-minded,
but it just might work.

273
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:32,357
As long as he doesn't see the
manuscript, Heaven's Door is powerless.

274
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,793
Come on, keep charging.

275
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:36,120
Hmm, a pretty good plan.

276
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:39,777
But all I have to do now is find
a way to force your eyes open.

277
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:40,690
Think fast!

278
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:45,850
What's this?

279
00:14:45,933 --> 00:14:47,317
He's powering through the pain.

280
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:49,857
If he keeps charging at
me like a stampeding bull,

281
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:51,737
things are going to get very ugly.

282
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:55,517
If I were a manga protagonist,
what would I do in this situation?

283
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,071
How would I get my enemy to open his eyes?

284
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,020
Keep going, Josuke!

285
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,200
Repeat, think, hurry up!

286
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:03,750
That's it.

287
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:07,115
Surely something in Koichi's
file will be able to help.

288
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:08,230
There!

289
00:15:08,313 --> 00:15:09,240
Exactly what I needed!

290
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:14,380
It seems certain comments set you
off, such as your hair is laughable.

291
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:18,617
Or wasn't that pincushion on your
head in fashion like two decades ago?

292
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:21,700
Or maybe you think that
hair looks cool, don't you?

293
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:22,670
How's that?

294
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:27,080
I guess remarks like those
really do set him off.

295
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:31,519
I must admit it's hard to believe,
but the files are always accurate.

296
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:34,320
What a preposterous Achilles' heel.

297
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,160
What the hell?

298
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,740
Did you say? Huh?

299
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:42,160
Just take it easy, Josuke!

300
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:45,140
I dare you to insult my hair again!

301
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,600
If you insist.

302
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,070
Fine.

303
00:15:48,153 --> 00:15:48,983
Here goes.

304
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:51,177
You might think your hair looks cool,

305
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,837
but in actuality, it may
be the shittiest hairstyle!

306
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:57,060
I've ever had the misfortune
of laying eyes upon!

307
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,180
Though to be fair?

308
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:01,257
That nest atop your useless noggin!

309
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:04,437
and may come in handy should a
pigeon come by and decide to roost.

310
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,700
But that's a very strong may.

311
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:15,120
Now witness heaven's door!

312
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,520
I win.

313
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,070
Point!

314
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,960
How the...

315
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,420
How is this happening?

316
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:37,797
I'm certain his eyes were open and he
got a full flash of the manuscript!

317
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:40,409
So why hasn't my
stanzibility taken effect?

318
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,260
We're back to normal! You're right!

319
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,980
I know I showed him the page. So what?

320
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,540
Where the hell did you slither off to?

321
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:00,380
Get out of here, you punk bitch!

322
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:03,817
Hey, I don't think he can
see straight right now.

323
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:04,730
Can't see?

324
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:07,617
Hold on, are you trying to
say Rohan's stupid insults?

325
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:11,457
Worked him up so much that he
doesn't even realize what he's doing?

326
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:14,060
Come on out, you manga-obsessed asshole!

327
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:15,680
I got a story for you!

328
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:19,397
It doesn't matter if it's from
a comic or someone's mouth.

329
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:23,320
If he hears any kind of hair
insult, he flies into a blind rage.

330
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:26,890
Incredible!

331
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:29,177
I had no idea his temper was this bad.

332
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:32,848
I don't think I've seen anything
like this in my entire life.

333
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:34,640
What the hell?

334
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:43,220
This is a facet of Josuke's personality
that even Koichi knew nothing about,

335
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:46,017
so it wasn't in his file
like everything else.

336
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,747
Though I still don't get it.

337
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:50,280
Why does he get so upset over his hair?

338
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,100
There has to be a reason.

339
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:54,080
But what is it?

340
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:57,557
Whoever insults my hair will
get the full brunt of my fury.

341
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,522
I won't stand for that bullshit!

342
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:01,257
Now that I think about it,

343
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:03,437
I'm positive Josuke told
me the reason behind his

344
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,677
freak-outs when it comes to
people insulting his hair,

345
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:07,557
but it's kind of an involved story.

346
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,470
Huh?

347
00:18:08,553 --> 00:18:09,897
What are you talking about?

348
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:13,760
It all happened when Josuke
was a little kid, and uh...

349
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:18,297
I'll try to remember
the story as best I can,

350
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:21,439
but I might have to fill
in some gaps along the way.

351
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:29,077
Josuke was 4 years old, and he'd passed
out from an inexplicably high fever.

352
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:32,800
For 50 days, no one knew
whether he would live or die.

353
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:35,290
Josuke

354
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:42,257
He found out later on that all of this
happened right around the time Jotaro and Mr.

355
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:44,537
Joestar were in Egypt
They traveled there in

356
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:47,385
order to defeat a heinous
stand user named Dio.

357
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,677
Josuke's mom had no
idea what was happening?

358
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:51,877
So she loaded him in the car and headed to

359
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:54,431
a hospital in S-City as fast as she could.

360
00:18:54,740 --> 00:18:59,211
But at the time, Morioh was in the
middle of its worst blizzard in 18 years.

361
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:01,160
No use.

362
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,380
What do I do?

363
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,913
Nobody ever uses this back road anymore.

364
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:10,492
And there's not a damn payphone in sight.

365
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:11,920
I'm an idiot.

366
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,217
I should have called for an ambulance.

367
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,477
Why did I bring Josuke out in the snow?

368
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:17,795
What's wrong with me?

369
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:21,407
And that's when it happened.

370
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:29,757
Hey, what the hell do you want?

371
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,369
Just go away, you creeper!

372
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,720
Got it.

373
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:16,940
Thank you so much!

374
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:27,930
Eventually,

375
00:20:28,013 --> 00:20:32,417
his mom tried to search for the young man,
but she couldn't find any trace of him.

376
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:35,797
While the stranger may not have
personally saved his life that night,

377
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:38,417
as far as four-year-old
Josuke was concerned,

378
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:43,029
that young man he encountered was a hero
unlike anyone he'd ever seen before.

379
00:20:43,340 --> 00:20:45,717
He became Josuke's role
model and a shining

380
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,447
example of what it means
to be a good person.

381
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:53,682
When someone insults that part of him, it
triggers something deep inside his heart.

382
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:56,764
I still don't know who
he is or where he's from.

383
00:20:57,180 --> 00:21:01,277
But in honor of him coming to our
rescue, I decided to adopt his hairstyle.

384
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:04,817
No one is allowed to disrespect
it, no matter who they are.

385
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:07,606
Disrespecting my hair
means disrespecting him.

386
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:11,357
As far as I'm aware, that's the
reason he flies off the handle.

387
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:14,077
But I have to admit, I thought
Josuke was just making it up,

388
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,577
so I wasn't listening very carefully.

389
00:21:15,660 --> 00:21:16,490
Huh.

390
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:18,307
I've never heard that story.

391
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:21,450
Careful!

392
00:21:21,533 --> 00:21:23,580
Rohan's holding a pen! You master!

393
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:25,417
Don't know when to call it quits, do ya?

394
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:26,330
No, that's not it.

395
00:21:26,413 --> 00:21:31,041
I wanted to make sure I wrote down that
beautiful story before I lost consciousness.

396
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,300
What a tale. Bravo.

397
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:36,140
I had an amazing experience to boot.

398
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:37,360
I'm overjoyed.

399
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:40,437
Experiences like this
happen once in a lifetime.

400
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:41,960
Such great inspiration.

401
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,740
How lucky am I.

402
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:48,760
I'm so glad I packed my bags and
moved to Morioh. It's no use.

403
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:51,437
As long as he's alive, he'll keep
searching for manga material,

404
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,557
even if he ends up battered and bruised.

405
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:56,197
At this point, you have to
commend his determination.

406
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,077
Putting aside good and bad for a minute,

407
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:01,417
he has one of the most admirable
work ethics I've ever seen.

408
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:04,029
Rohan-sensei is truly
a super manga artist.

409
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:06,320
I finally found you, manga artist!

410
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:09,780
Last I checked, I wasn't
done punching you!

411
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:14,220
His determination is
pretty commendable, too.

412
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:15,710
Um, yeah.

413
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,060
Due to an unforeseen illness,

414
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:26,107
Rohan Kishibe's Pink Dark Boy
will be on hiatus for one month.

415
00:23:10,433 --> 00:23:12,888
Get closer, breathe in
and get a bit higher.

416
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:17,080
You'll never know what
hit you when I get to you.

417
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:24,480
Ooh, I want you, I don't know if I
need you, but ooh, I gotta find you.

418
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:26,890
Ooh,

419
00:23:26,980 --> 00:23:33,380
I want you, I don't know if I need
you, but ooh, I gotta find you.

420
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:40,610
SmackDown!
